<p>The variable <strong>joy1</strong> (all lowercase) is filled in by a call to
<strong>readjoy1()</strong>. It holds five flags, one per direction plus the fire
button, for the joystick in port 1. A bit is 1 while that direction or button
is <strong>currently held</strong>.</p>
<p>Test it with the JOY_UP, JOY_LEFT, JOY_DOWN, JOY_RIGHT and JOY_FIRE masks.
Their bit values are not the same on every machine, so always use the constants
rather than raw numbers.</p>
<p>readjoy1() also fills in <strong>joy1pressed</strong>, which reports only the
frame a direction was first pressed, and <strong>joy1last</strong>, the previous
frame's reading.</p>

<p>Example</p>
<code>
readjoy1();

if (joy1 &amp; JOY_UP)    then y := y - 1;
if (joy1 &amp; JOY_DOWN)  then y := y + 1;
if (joy1 &amp; JOY_LEFT)  then x := x - 1;
if (joy1 &amp; JOY_RIGHT) then x := x + 1;
if (joy1 &amp; JOY_FIRE)  then Shoot();
</code>
<p>See also joy1pressed and readjoy1.</p>
